  "notes": "Official cause code and category are TBD/provisional in FORM-366 FIELDS despite the narrative clearly identifying 'Electrical Contact Degradation' as the direct cause; per rule 4 we preserve TBD/provisional and set provisional=true, capturing the narrative's cause statement in proximate_text/theme. No block_13 rows were provided. No previous similar occurrences were cited (narrative explicitly states none), so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge was created. HPCI was determined to remain available/functional throughout per Technical Evaluation, but was retroactively determined to have met inoperability criteria under TS 3.3.5.1 Action D.1 due to the common-mode relay issue affecting both channels — modeled as a Consequence reflecting the missed required declaration/TS entry rather than an actual loss of function. Manual operation of the ISV via the relay contact was unaffected, so HPCI retained a manual backstop, but this is design/procedural context rather than a distinct backup system and was not modeled as a System node."
